  "notes": "Not to be confused with the homophone {選挙|せんきょ} (election). {占拠|せんきょ} uses {占|せん} (occupy/seize).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {不法|ふほう}{占拠|せんきょ}: illegal occupation, squatting\n- {武力|ぶりょく}{占拠|せんきょ}: armed seizure\n- {市場|しじょう}を{占拠|せんきょ}する: to dominate a market\n- {建物|たてもの}を{占拠|せんきょ}する: to occupy a building\n\nUSAGE:\nOften appears in news about protests, military actions, or territorial disputes. Can also be used figuratively for market dominance.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {占領|せんりょう}: military occupation (larger scale, e.g. a country)\n- {占有|せんゆう}: possession, occupancy (legal term)\n- {制圧|せいあつ}: suppression, gaining control by force",
